  "notes": "A layout for a room that stands on its own (no parent): a box at the origin of its own plane, 0, 0 on storey 0. constants: the band table of data/location/size.yml (default, and each sort's width and depth in whole paces, lowest first, both ends included) and the four sides in order. A case is one of six asks. sides: the bands a room of kind is sized from; a kind that is null or not in the table takes the default. size: width then depth, each low + Random#rand(high - low + 1) from one generator seeded Roll(story, sequence: room, kind: ROOM_SIZE = 20). side: which side the way out (its location_connections id) leaves by: sides[Random#rand(4)] from Roll(story, sequence: way, kind: WAY_OUT_SIDE = 21), worked out on every read and never kept. beside: the cell of room beside side, that side's middle cell, the western or northern of two (x + (width - 1) div 2, y + (depth - 1) div 2). by_the_way_out: beside(room, side(story, way)). lay_out: a story and every row its records hold (locations, items, characters); output is, in id order, each of the story's rooms with no parent and neither a box nor a footprint, with its box (the size above, at the origin) and, by id, a spot for each of the world's own things lying loose on its floor (no playthrough, no holder, not within a piece) and each person in it but the protagonist that has no spot yet, as Placement rolls one in the world (Roll(story, sequence: id, kind: ITEM_POSITION or CHARACTER_POSITION), x then y inside the box).",
